  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Africa Rural Climate Adaptation Finance Mechanism (ARCAFIM) for East Africa region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ARCAFIM aims to scale up private sector climate change adaptation finance in East Africa through an on-lending programme that supports smallholders and rural micro, small and medium-sized enterprises (MSMEs) involved in food systems to invest in climate resilient technologies and practices.

&#x2022; The programme mainstreams climate change adaptation finance in East Africa in the food system which is a nascent sector and therefore support sustainable agriculture, food and water security, resilient livelihoods and improved sustainable land use. 
&#x2022; It de-risks investment through a risk-sharing structure that unlocks international capital and mobilizes regional private capital.
&#x2022; It empowers participating financial institutions, smallholders and rural MSMEs by providing them with technical assistance and capacity-building.</narrative>
  </description>
